Remove a solid chroma-key background and write an image with alpha.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --input INPUT         Input image path.
  --out OUT             Output .png or .webp path.
  --key-color KEY_COLOR
                        Hex RGB key color to remove, for example #00ff00.
  --tolerance TOLERANCE
                        Hard-key per-channel tolerance for matching the key
                        color, 0-255.
  --auto-key {none,corners,border}
                        Sample the key color from image corners or border
                        instead of --key-color.
  --soft-matte          Use a smooth alpha ramp between transparent and opaque
                        thresholds.
  --transparent-threshold TRANSPARENT_THRESHOLD
                        Soft-matte distance at or below which pixels become
                        fully transparent.
  --opaque-threshold OPAQUE_THRESHOLD
                        Soft-matte distance at or above which pixels become
                        fully opaque.
  --edge-feather EDGE_FEATHER
                        Optional alpha blur radius for softened edges, 0-64.
  --edge-contract EDGE_CONTRACT
                        Shrink the visible alpha matte by this many pixels
                        before feathering.
  --spill-cleanup       Reduce obvious key-color spill on opaque pixels.
  --despill             Alias for --spill-cleanup; decontaminate key-color
                        edge spill.
  --force               Overwrite an existing output file.

